# Explicit semgrep ignore list (issue #98).
#
# DECISION: tests/ IS scanned. Semgrep's built-in default ignore list
# excludes tests/ entirely, which made the documented "semgrep on tests"
# gate factually empty (0 files scanned, verified in sprint 30). Test code
# handles subprocesses, temp files and fixtures — exactly the API surface
# the security rules cover. Ruff's S-rules (bandit) already run on tests
# with S101 (assert) exempted; semgrep complements them here.
#
# This file REPLACES semgrep's defaults, so everything to skip must be
# listed explicitly.

# Virtual envs / caches / build artifacts
.venv/
.git/
.mutmut-cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
dist/
build/

# Mutation staging area (generated copies, never reviewed source)
mutants/

# All Sdist-shipped E2E fixtures are scanned.  Some started as upstream
# reference fixtures, while stress_test, simple_lib, and source_layout are
# project-authored; one broad exclusion hid both classes and was not a safe
# release boundary.

# Gitignored scratchpad for one-off verification scripts
_issues/

